In https://github.com/httpwg/http-extensions/pull/1420, RFC 6265bis was modified to specify truncation of set-cookie-lines at the first {CR, LF, NUL} byte. This is consistent with Chrome's current behavior.

@annevk [points out](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/28290#issuecomment-818826795) that this may enable an attack where an attacker may inject a CR, LF, or NUL byte into a cookie value to cause its truncation, thus changing the value of the cookie.

Investigate interop/web compatibility and consider rejecting all cookies containing any control character (rather than truncating).

