I tried to reproduce the digest from the example in Section 6 to double-check my understanding of content, representation, and unencoded representation. Here's a quick Node.js script to demonstrate what I did:

```js
const crypto = require('crypto')
const zlib = require('zlib')
const assert = require('assert')

// Representation from figure 2
const repr = Buffer.from([
    0x1f, 0x8b, 0x08, 0x00, 0x79, 0x1f, 0x08, 0x64, 0x00, 0xff,
    0x73, 0xcc, 0x53, 0x28, 0xcd, 0x4b, 0xad, 0x48, 0x4e, 0x2d,
    0x28, 0xc9, 0xcc, 0xcf, 0x4b, 0xcc, 0x51, 0x28, 0x2e, 0x29,
    0xca, 0xcc, 0x4b, 0xe7, 0x02, 0x00, 0x7e, 0xaf, 0x07, 0x44,
    0x18, 0x00, 0x00, 0x00,
])

// Decode the representation
const unencoded = zlib.gunzipSync(repr).toString('utf8')
assert.equal(unencoded, 'An unexceptional string\n') // ok

// Check Unencoded-Digest
const unencodedDigest = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(unencoded).digest('base64')
assert.equal(unencodedDigest, '5Bv3NIx05BPnh0jMph6v1RJ5Q7kl9LKMtQxmvc9+Z7Y=') // ok

// Check Content-Digest of partial response
const partialContent = repr.subarray(0, 10)
const contentDigest = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(partialContent).digest('base64')
assert.equal(contentDigest, 'SotB7Pa5A7iHSBdh9mg1Ev/ktAzrxU4Z8ldcCIUyfI4=') // ok

// Check Repr-Digest
const reprDigest = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(repr).digest('base64')
assert.equal(reprDigest, 'XyjvEuFb1P5rqc2le3vQm7M96DwZhvmOwqHLu2xVpY4=') // failure
```

The unencoded representation, Unencoded-Digest, and Content-Digest are the same as in the draft, but I cannot get the same Repr-Digest. It produces `kwcdt3RBGcsLaj7QSz9AW8MuwJaLjOJqUU/jKixF2oU=` instead of `XyjvEuFb1P5rqc2le3vQm7M96DwZhvmOwqHLu2xVpY4=` from the draft.

